@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+---
+title: Screenshots and media information
+description: Configure screenshot formats and filename templates, capture subtitle-inclusive frames, and inspect complete media metadata.
+---
+
+## Screenshot settings
+
+mpvRx can save PNG, JPEG, and supported WebP output. Settings include lossy quality, PNG compression, WebP lossless mode, filename template, and whether rendered subtitles are included.
+
+Native mpv capture is attempted first. Compatible formats can fall back to an Android image conversion path when native output is unavailable.
+
+Screenshots are saved under the Pictures media collection in the `mpvSnaps` folder on modern Android versions.
+
+## Filename placeholders
+
+| Placeholder | Value |
+| --- | --- |
+| `%Y` | Four-digit year |
+| `%m` | Month |
+| `%d` | Day |
+| `%H` | Hour |
+| `%M` | Minute |
+| `%S` | Second |
+| `%f` | Source filename with extension |
+| `%F` | Source filename without extension |
+| `%P` | Playback position as `HH:MM:SS.mmm` |
+| `%p` | Playback position as `HH:MM:SS` |
+| `%wH` | Playback-position hours |
+| `%wM` | Playback-position minutes |
+| `%wS` | Playback-position seconds |
+| `%wT` | Playback-position milliseconds |
+
+Default template:
+
+```text
+mpv_snapshot_%Y%m%d_%H%M%S
+```
+
+Invalid filename characters are replaced, excess whitespace is normalized, and generated names are capped to a safe length.
+
+## Frame Review snapshots
+
+Frame Review can capture the exact reviewed position and independently choose subtitle inclusion. See [Precision playback tools](/docs/playback/precision-playback-tools).
+
+## Media information
+
+The media information view organizes parsed metadata by kind:
+
+- Container/general details and system path
+- Video, audio, text/subtitle, image, and other tracks
+- Programs, timecode tracks, and MKV attachments
+- Raw MediaInfo report
+
+Images and embedded cover art receive image-specific fields such as resolution, format, bit depth, color space, compression, and orientation. Tap a value to open its complete selectable text and copy it without truncation.
+
+Use the Raw tab when preparing a codec/container report, but review paths, titles, server URLs, and tags for private information before sharing it.
diff --git a/website/content/docs/advanced/secure-folder.mdx b/website/content/docs/advanced/secure-folder.mdx
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..86fb26e6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/website/content/docs/advanced/secure-folder.mdx
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+---
+title: Secure Folder
+description: Set up protected media, use biometric unlock, move and restore items, hide the entry point, and recover a forgotten PIN.
+---
+
+Secure Folder limits casual access to selected local media on a shared device. It is an app-level access-control feature, not a replacement for Android device encryption.
+
+## Initial setup
+
+The first visit requires:
+
+1. A four-digit PIN
+2. A non-empty recovery question
+3. A non-empty recovery answer
+
+The PIN and normalized recovery answer are stored as salted hashes. Choose an answer you can reproduce later; capitalization and surrounding spaces are normalized during verification.
+
+## Unlock and biometrics
+
+After setup, enter the PIN to unlock. Biometric authentication can be enabled when Android reports a supported enrolled method. Android handles the biometric prompt; mpvRx does not receive biometric data.
+
+## Move media into Secure Folder
+
+Select individual media or one or more folders in the local browser, then choose the Secure Folder action. Folder moves resolve all contained videos before processing.
+
+The result reports successful and failed item counts. A partial result means some files moved while others remained, commonly because their storage providers or permissions differ.
+
+## Restore or delete
+
+Inside Secure Folder, select items to restore them to normal storage or delete them. Confirmation prompts can be disabled separately for move, restore, delete, and hiding the entry point.
+
+Review the selected count before destructive actions. Deleting from Secure Folder removes the underlying media; it is not merely removed from the protected index.
+
+## Hide the entry point
+
+The Secure Folder row can be hidden from Settings after confirmation. Hidden entry does not encrypt files or remove the need for a PIN; it only reduces casual discoverability. Keep a known recovery path before hiding it.
+
+## Forgot PIN
+
+The recovery flow verifies the stored security answer before allowing a replacement PIN. The existing PIN remains valid until the new PIN is successfully saved, so abandoning recovery cannot leave the folder open for a new setup.
+
+:::warning
+If both PIN and recovery answer are lost, mpvRx cannot derive them from their hashes. Keep device backups and do not treat Secure Folder as the only copy of important media.
+:::
diff --git a/website/content/docs/advanced/syncplay.mdx b/website/content/docs/advanced/syncplay.mdx
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..6fdae672
--- /dev/null
+++ b/website/content/docs/advanced/syncplay.mdx
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+---
+title: Syncplay rooms
+description: Connect to a Syncplay server and synchronize pause, seek, position, and readiness with a room.
+---
+
+Syncplay coordinates playback state between people who already have access to equivalent media. It does not send the video file to other participants.
+
+## Connection fields
+
+| Field | Requirement |
+| --- | --- |
+| Host | Non-empty Syncplay server hostname or IP address |
+| Port | `1` through `65535`; the public default is `8999` |
+| Username | Non-empty room display name |
+| Room | Non-empty room identifier shared by participants |
+| Password | Optional room password |
+
+The built-in defaults point to `syncplay.pl:8999`, username `MpvRxUser`, and room `TestRoom`. Replace the room and username before real use.
+
+## Join a room
+
+1. Open the Syncplay connection screen.
+2. Enter the same server, room, and password as the other participants.
+3. Choose a distinct username.
+4. Connect and wait for login to complete.
+5. Open the matching media and mark readiness when the room workflow requires it.
+
+Connection details are saved for reconnect. The password is part of those saved credentials, so do not reuse a sensitive account password as a room password.
+
+## What synchronizes
+
+mpvRx exchanges file identity, playback position, pause state, readiness, controller state, and timing information. Latency estimates are used to compensate for network delay and avoid reacting to the client's own echoed updates.
+
+Remote pause and seek events control the active playback session. Local state changes are sent back to the room after login.
+
+## Media matching
+
+Every participant should load the same cut and duration. Similar filenames do not guarantee identical timing. Different intros, frame rates, edits, or chapter layouts can stay offset even when the room position is synchronized.
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+- **Cannot connect:** verify host, port, DNS, firewall, and server availability.
+- **Login fails:** confirm room password and remove accidental spaces.
+- **Position drifts:** compare file duration and edition across participants.
+- **Repeated reconnect:** test without VPN or mobile network switching.
+- **Wrong media:** leave the room, load the intended file, and reconnect.
